    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0297" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/874</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitlock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Havre</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-03T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 3, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 4, 10.35
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. Your 285, September 28, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d281-f1"/> and my 94,
                    September 30, 1 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d281-f2"/> Baron de Broqueville
                    returned from the front to-day. He authorizes the following statement: “If that
                    note is true it is an insolence added to the injury already done Belgium.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitlock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
